## Conventions in this repo

- `from qm.qua import *` is standard here; do not flag it as a lint issue.
- Match existing patterns in the nearest folder (standalone script vs qualibration node).
- Format/lint: `uv run black .` and `uv run ruff check .` per [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).

## QUA 1.3.1 / 1.4.0 migration

When updating QUA programs, follow [docs/plans/qua-1.4.0-migration.md](../../docs/plans/qua-1.4.0-migration.md) (API reference) and [docs/plans/qua-1.4.0-migration-runbook.md](../../docs/plans/qua-1.4.0-migration-runbook.md) (step-by-step playbook for all QCA modalities).

**Cross-modality / new repo:** Migration scripts accept `--modality` (e.g. `Quantum-Dots`, `AMO`, `Optically addressable spin qubits`) or `--qca-root`. Bootstrap a modality fork via [docs/bootstrap/MANIFEST.md](../../docs/bootstrap/MANIFEST.md) and `scripts/bootstrap_modality_repo.sh`.

**Part 1 (1.3.1)** — prefer **iterables + auto-streaming** for sweep experiments:
- [Iterables & Auto-Streaming (1.3.1)](https://docs.quantum-machines.co/1.3.1/docs/Guides/qua_iterables/)
- [qm-qua 1.3.1 release notes](https://docs.quantum-machines.co/1.3.1/docs/Releases/qm_qua_releases/)

Use `declare_output_stream()` instead of deprecated `declare_stream()`.
Use native QUA 1.3.1 iterables and `declare_with_stream` directly in calibration nodes (see migration plan template).
Frequency/detuning sweep arrays passed to `QuaIterable` and used with `update_frequency` must be **`.astype(int)`** (Hz integers); `coerce_to_integer=True` on `unit()` is not enough when `np.arange` stop/step promotes float dtype.

**Part 2 (1.4.0)** — controller / logical config split. When editing configuration files or QM open/execute call sites, follow the **Controller / logical config split** section in the guide.

- [Configuration split overview](https://docs.quantum-machines.co/latest/docs/Introduction/config/) — controller vs logical keys
- **Execute / compile:** `open_qm(controller_config)`; pass `logical_config` to `execute` / `compile`
- **Simulate:** `qmm.simulate(merge_qua_config(...), ...)` on the manager — **never** `open_qm` before simulate ([OPX Simulator](https://docs.quantum-machines.co/latest/docs/Guides/simulator/))
- `mixers` belongs to **controller** config (not logical)

**Part 3 (1.4.0)** — do **not** use `pulse * amp(scale)` in new QUA code. Pass `amplitude_scale=` to `play` and `measure` instead. See the **`amp()` deprecation** section in the guide.

**Part 4 (1.4.0)** — do **not** use `add_to_queue(..., overrides=...)` or `queue.add_compiled()`. Prefer `qm.execute(program, config=logical_config)`.
